  "tagline": "Oracle's engineered system for Oracle Database, with smart storage offload for OLTP and analytics.",
  "description": "Exadata is Oracle's co-engineered hardware and software platform for Oracle Database. Its storage servers run Exadata System Software that pushes SQL filtering, Hybrid Columnar Compression, storage indexes and AI vector search offload down to storage, connected over RDMA, so one platform handles demanding OLTP and data warehousing together. It is sold on-premises, as Cloud@Customer, as Exadata Database Service and Autonomous Database in OCI, and inside AWS, Azure and Google Cloud via Oracle Database@. It is the high-end choice for Oracle shops; cost and lock-in are the trade-offs.",
